      "writtenOn": "2024-03-26T09:39:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is always using the \"WW\" code every time we need to (re-)start ot-daemon. Instead, we should use the latest country code from the ThreadNetworkCountryCode#getCountryCode() API. To do that, you don\u0027t need to add a dependency on the ThreadNetworkCountryCode class, but simply add a Supplier. For example:\n\n```\nThreadNetworkControllerService(\n            Context context,\n            Handler handler,\n            NetworkProvider networkProvider,\n            Supplier\u003cIOtDaemon\u003e otDaemonSupplier,\n            ConnectivityManager connectivityManager,\n            TunInterfaceController tunIfController,\n            InfraInterfaceController infraIfController,\n            ThreadPersistentSettings persistentSettings,\n            NsdPublisher nsdPublisher,\n            UserManager userManager,\n            ConnectivityResources resources,\n            Supplier\u003cString\u003e countryCodeSupplier) {\n              mCountryCodeSupplier \u003d countryCodeSupplier;\n            }\n            \n            \n        otDaemon.initialize(\n                mTunIfController.getTunFd(),\n                isEnabled(),\n                mNsdPublisher,\n                getMeshcopTxtAttributes(mResources.get()),\n                mOtDaemonCallbackProxy,\n                mCountryCodeSupplier.get());\n```\n\nAnd the ThreadNetworkControllerService can be instantiated with:\n\n```\nThreadNetworkControllerService.newInstance(\n    mContext, mSettings, mCountryCode::getCountryCode);\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 409,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 409,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "c65c461b3a9458b753a5e6ff0be1f25b4cde5040",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
